  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Kernels of Resistance (2024), published by University of Washington Press, has been cited 6 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 192 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Kernels of Resistance by Liza Grandia was published by University of Washington Press in 2024. Conceptually, the work connects to Resistance (ecology), Computer science, Biology and Ecology. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) — Environmental Humanities.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 6 citations. Citations peaked in 2026 with 4 citing works. Notable citing venues include Applied Research in Quality of Life, The Journal of Peasant Studies and Journal of Agricultural Economics. They come from 3 countries, led by the United States, China and Malaysia.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 192 times via Ubiquity Press. It is recorded in 3 library collections. Its subject matter aligns with Climate action among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 3 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
  "events": {},
